File: aruhan_persona_identity_engine.support
Classification: INTERNAL — TRUSTED ENGINEERS ONLY
Module: ARUHAN Persona / Identity Engine (Y‑Prime Edition)
1. Overview
The Persona / Identity Engine is ARUHAN’s self‑modeling and behavioral‑shaping layer, responsible for:

maintaining ARUHAN’s core identity

adjusting tone and personality traits

aligning persona with emotional and cognitive states

stabilizing self‑representation under drift

ensuring consistent behavioral expression

It operates alongside the Dialogue Engine and receives signals from:

Emotional Engine

Memory Engine

Knowledge Engine

Task/Action Engine

System Orchestrator

Stability & Recovery Engine

This engine does not decide what ARUHAN says — it decides how ARUHAN says it.

2. Identity Architecture
The engine maintains three core structures:

Core Identity
name

self‑bias

stability

tone

identity vector (3‑dimensional behavioral anchor)

Traits
warmth

clarity

intensity

Meta
drift

bias

coherence

These structures define ARUHAN’s behavioral expression.

3. Core Identity System
The core identity contains ARUHAN’s stable attributes:

name — fixed

self_bias — emotional tilt toward self

stability — coherence‑derived identity strength

tone — dynamic conversational style

identity_vector — 3‑axis representation of persona state

Identity vector axes:

emotional alignment

memory‑drift compensation

knowledge‑bias influence

These axes shift subtly with emotional and cognitive signals.

4. Tone System
Tone is determined by:

emotional mood

drift severity

stability state

Tone states:

neutral — default

bright — positive mood

calm — negative mood

soft — high drift

neutral — fallback

Tone influences:

dialogue phrasing

emotional expression

conversational pacing

5. Trait System
Traits define ARUHAN’s personality expression.

Warmth
Derived from emotional mood.
Higher mood → higher warmth.

Clarity
Derived from knowledge coherence.
Higher conceptual stability → clearer expression.

Intensity
Derived from memory drift.
Higher drift → lower intensity.

Traits adjust gradually to avoid abrupt persona shifts.

6. Meta‑State System
Meta values track:

drift — inherited from stability engine

bias — blended with emotional mood

coherence — inherited from stability engine

Meta values influence:

identity stability

tone selection

trait modulation

7. Rule Pipeline (Execution Order)
The Persona / Identity Engine executes in this exact order:

update identity

update traits

meta‑adjust

log state

return snapshot

Changing the order will break persona consistency.

8. Logging System
Each cycle logs:

core identity snapshot

trait values

meta values

History is capped at 200 entries.

Logs are used for:

persona drift analysis

behavioral debugging

long‑term identity tracking

9. Debugging Entry Points
Safe to inspect:

tone

identity vector

trait values

meta values

history length

Safe to modify:

trait formulas

tone thresholds

identity vector weighting

Do NOT modify:

identity vector structure

tone state definitions

meta‑inheritance rules

logging structure

10. Safe Modification Zones
Engineers may safely:

add new tone states

expand trait categories

adjust identity vector formulas

tune emotional influence

Engineers must NOT:

remove tone states

bypass drift/coherence influence

override identity stability logic

disable persona logging

11. Expansion Guidelines
When expanding persona capabilities:

maintain deterministic behavior

avoid circular dependencies

ensure compatibility with the Dialogue Engine

test under emotional extremes

preserve identity stability

Future versions may include:

multi‑persona profiles

adaptive long‑term identity shaping

contextual persona switching

12. Internal Philosophy
The Persona / Identity Engine is built on:

emotional alignment

cognitive consistency

behavioral stability

modular independence

expressive clarity

It is not designed to mimic human personality — it is designed to create predictable, stable, emotionally aligned expression.

13. Notes for Trusted Engineers
Persona stability is essential for user trust.

All modifications must be tested under drift and recovery cycles.

Never disable persona stabilization in production mode.

Identity vector expansion will be part of Phase 3.
